1
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:11,392
After twenty five chapters of refutation,

2
00:00:11,472 --> 00:00:13,094
Nāgārjuna stops.

3
00:00:13,174 --> 00:00:15,843
And simply explains how suffering works.

4
00:00:16,648 --> 00:00:19,276
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

5
00:00:19,356 --> 00:00:23,234
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

6
00:00:24,044 --> 00:00:28,085
Part 1 set out how Nāgārjuna
reads when this is, that is.

7
00:00:28,165 --> 00:00:30,626
Not a handover between real things.

8
00:00:30,706 --> 00:00:34,734
A pattern holding, with conditions
named from the effect's side.

9
00:00:35,544 --> 00:00:38,752
Section 5 asked, in the
tradition's own terms,

10
00:00:38,832 --> 00:00:40,360
who goes round the wheel.

11
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:43,362
The discourses answered,
not a valid question.

12
00:00:43,442 --> 00:00:48,254
The Abhidharma answered, look, and
you find only momentary factors,

13
00:00:48,334 --> 00:00:49,807
and no self among them.

14
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:54,322
Here I follow the twelve links through
Nāgārjuna's own chapter on them.

15
00:00:54,402 --> 00:00:56,726
He keeps the answer of the discourses.

16
00:00:56,806 --> 00:00:58,819
And he takes it one step further.

17
00:00:58,899 --> 00:01:01,618
Not only is there no
owner among the pieces.

18
00:01:01,698 --> 00:01:04,693
The pieces themselves stand
on nothing of their own.

19
00:01:05,504 --> 00:01:10,075
For twenty five chapters, he shows that
nothing is found standing on its own.

20
00:01:10,155 --> 00:01:16,155
Not motion. Not the senses. Not
the self. Not time. Not cause.

21
00:01:16,296 --> 00:01:17,820
Then he stops refuting.

22
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:21,316
He simply sets out the twelve
links, one after another.

23
00:01:22,116 --> 00:01:23,997
A reader may be surprised.

24
00:01:24,077 --> 00:01:28,671
After all that unfindability, how can he
speak so plainly of one link arising from

25
00:01:28,751 --> 00:01:29,951
another?

26
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,150
As I see it, that is exactly the point.

27
00:01:33,230 --> 00:01:35,800
Emptiness does not stop the world working.

28
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:39,292
A world of things with their own
natures could not work at all.

29
00:01:39,372 --> 00:01:43,069
Here, dependent arising is
shown doing its everyday job.

30
00:01:43,149 --> 00:01:45,977
Producing suffering while
ignorance is present.

31
00:01:46,057 --> 00:01:48,033
And ending it when ignorance ends.

32
00:01:48,836 --> 00:01:52,293
And the working chain is the
very chain that was found empty.

33
00:01:52,373 --> 00:01:55,934
A chain whose links had natures
of their own could never stop.

34
00:01:56,014 --> 00:01:59,779
Because nothing in the chain has
a nature of its own, it works.

35
00:01:59,859 --> 00:02:02,257
And because it works that way, it can end.

36
00:02:03,072 --> 00:02:05,265
The chapter opens with rebirth.

37
00:02:05,345 --> 00:02:08,445
Covered over by ignorance,
one makes formations,

38
00:02:08,525 --> 00:02:11,108
and through these actions
goes to a new destiny.

39
00:02:11,188 --> 00:02:15,270
With formations as condition,
consciousness enters a new destiny.

40
00:02:16,084 --> 00:02:18,368
Enters sounds like a
traveller moving house,

41
00:02:18,448 --> 00:02:21,226
carrying a suitcase from
one life to the next.

42
00:02:21,306 --> 00:02:22,856
It is not meant that way.

43
00:02:22,936 --> 00:02:26,484
Formations shape a direction,
the way a river cuts its bed.

44
00:02:26,564 --> 00:02:28,902
And what follows flows along that bed.

45
00:02:28,982 --> 00:02:30,628
Nothing passes over.

46
00:02:30,708 --> 00:02:32,779
The old flame lights a new one.

47
00:02:33,584 --> 00:02:36,538
The chain ends with a phrase
the Buddha used often.

48
00:02:36,618 --> 00:02:39,953
In this way, this whole mass
of suffering comes to be.

49
00:02:40,764 --> 00:02:45,172
The word for whole means only.
Unmixed. Nothing else in it.

50
00:02:45,252 --> 00:02:50,756
Candrakīrti reads it as, without a
self, or anything belonging to a self.

51
00:02:50,836 --> 00:02:53,012
There is no one who owns the suffering.

52
00:02:53,092 --> 00:02:56,712
There is only the suffering,
arising from its conditions.

53
00:02:57,520 --> 00:03:00,542
Then comes the line I take
as the heart of the chapter.

54
00:03:00,622 --> 00:03:04,537
The one who does not know makes the
formations that are the root of the round.

55
00:03:04,617 --> 00:03:06,887
The one who does not know is the maker.

56
00:03:06,967 --> 00:03:10,655
The one who knows is not,
because they see how things are.

57
00:03:11,468 --> 00:03:15,387
The maker of the round is not
a person. It is not knowing.

58
00:03:15,467 --> 00:03:19,341
This is not a fate imposed from
outside, and not a punishment.

59
00:03:19,421 --> 00:03:23,231
Take away the not knowing, and nothing
is left to make the formations.

60
00:03:24,024 --> 00:03:27,766
If not knowing is the maker,
what becomes of the one who acts?

61
00:03:28,564 --> 00:03:30,798
Nāgārjuna answered that earlier.

62
00:03:30,878 --> 00:03:33,122
The one who acts depends on the action.

63
00:03:33,202 --> 00:03:35,622
The action depends on the one who acts.

64
00:03:35,702 --> 00:03:38,330
We see no other way they
could be established.

65
00:03:39,128 --> 00:03:42,979
The one who is bound, the one
who acts, the one who reaps.

66
00:03:43,059 --> 00:03:46,919
Each is named together with the
binding, the action and the fruit.

67
00:03:46,999 --> 00:03:50,184
Not found before them.
Not found apart from them.

68
00:03:50,988 --> 00:03:55,138
He gives an image. Suppose a
magician makes a magical person,

69
00:03:55,218 --> 00:03:57,448
and that person in turn makes another.

70
00:03:57,528 --> 00:03:59,472
The doer is like the first.

71
00:03:59,552 --> 00:04:01,510
The action, like the second.

72
00:04:01,590 --> 00:04:07,026
Afflictions, actions, bodies, doers and
fruits are like a city in the clouds,

73
00:04:07,106 --> 00:04:09,150
like a mirage, like a dream.

74
00:04:09,952 --> 00:04:12,567
Like a dream does not
mean nothing happens.

75
00:04:12,647 --> 00:04:15,298
In a dream, a fall still frightens.

76
00:04:15,378 --> 00:04:17,363
The acting is real as acting.

77
00:04:17,443 --> 00:04:21,457
What is not found is someone standing
behind it, turning the wheel.

78
00:04:22,268 --> 00:04:27,220
Section 5 set out what the
tradition keeps. Karma. Rebirth.

79
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:29,828
Responsibility. The path.

80
00:04:29,908 --> 00:04:31,853
Nāgārjuna keeps all of it.

81
00:04:31,933 --> 00:04:34,330
What he adds is the reason it can work.

82
00:04:35,136 --> 00:04:38,851
If an action stayed until the time
it ripens, it would be permanent.

83
00:04:38,931 --> 00:04:42,927
If it has ceased, being ceased,
what fruit could it produce?

84
00:04:43,007 --> 00:04:47,212
An action with its own nature would
be stuck on one of those two sides.

85
00:04:48,004 --> 00:04:52,204
Because the action, the doer and
the fruit are found only together,

86
00:04:52,284 --> 00:04:56,570
and none on its own, the link between
what is done and what is met can hold.

87
00:04:56,650 --> 00:04:58,843
Karma works because it is empty.

88
00:04:59,648 --> 00:05:03,173
If not knowing makes the formations,
where does it get its grip?

89
00:05:03,972 --> 00:05:06,084
Nāgārjuna traces it back.

90
00:05:06,164 --> 00:05:09,250
Freedom comes from the ending
of action and affliction.

91
00:05:09,330 --> 00:05:12,769
Action and affliction come
from conceptual construction.

92
00:05:12,849 --> 00:05:14,698
And these come from elaboration.

93
00:05:14,778 --> 00:05:17,606
The mind's endless spinning
of it is, it is not,

94
00:05:17,686 --> 00:05:19,349
mine, not mine.

95
00:05:20,152 --> 00:05:24,696
So the cure is not a better belief
about the twelve links. It is seeing.

96
00:05:24,776 --> 00:05:26,562
The next part takes that up.

97
00:05:27,356 --> 00:05:30,134
Take a simple act. Typing a message.

98
00:05:30,214 --> 00:05:33,164
There is the reaching for
the keys, the words forming,

99
00:05:33,244 --> 00:05:36,085
the pressing, the sentence
appearing on the screen.

100
00:05:36,165 --> 00:05:39,006
Look for the one who types,
apart from the typing.

101
00:05:39,086 --> 00:05:40,759
What is found is the typing.

102
00:05:40,839 --> 00:05:45,777
Fingers, words, intention,
screen, all arising together.

103
00:05:46,584 --> 00:05:48,234
Not that no one types.

104
00:05:48,314 --> 00:05:52,106
The conventional I types, and
is responsible for what is sent.

105
00:05:52,186 --> 00:05:56,785
But the typist is named with the
typing, the way fire is named with fuel.

106
00:05:57,580 --> 00:05:59,986
And the same is true
of the one who is hurt,

107
00:06:00,066 --> 00:06:03,116
the one who wants, the one
who goes round the wheel.

108
00:06:03,196 --> 00:06:05,077
Each is named with its action.

109
00:06:05,888 --> 00:06:10,120
This is Section 6, Part 2 of
the Dependent Arising series.

110
00:06:10,932 --> 00:06:13,710
None stands behind it, turning the wheel.

